# [[.Name]]

A game made with [Veduta](https://github.com/riftbane/veduta) [[.Engine]], in Lua, for the
Veduta console: a handheld with a 320×240 panel, a D-pad, A, B, Select, Cancel and Home.

## Play

Download `[[.Name]]_<version>.tar.gz` from the project's GitHub Releases and unpack it onto
the console's card: the `[[.Name]]` folder it contains is the game, with its `card.json`,
and the console lists it by that.

## Develop

```sh
veduta build                     # checks the scripts
veduta test                      # every scenario in tests/scenarios
veduta simulate --scenario tests/scenarios/start.scenario.json
veduta render --scene main --out out/main.png
veduta doctor
veduta release v0.1.0            # tag; GitHub Actions publishes the archive
```

No Go and no build: the `veduta` tool runs the game itself. The project is set up for
Claude Code: `claude` in this directory connects to the `veduta` MCP server (see
`.mcp.json`) and follows `CLAUDE.md`.

Layout: `veduta.json` (manifest), `card.json` (what the console lists), `main.lua` (the
game), `assets/` (JSON sources for models, textures, materials and scenes),
`tests/scenarios/` (deterministic scenario tests).
